c:Ta28,{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"How many total Paras (Juz) and pages are in the Holy Quran?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"The Holy Quran contains 30 Paras (Juz) and 114 Surahs. In the standard King Fahd Complex Madani Mushaf (15-line Uthmani script), there are exactly 604 pages, structured so that each Juz comprises 20 pages (with the 30th Juz covering 23 pages). Indo-Pak 16-line editions generally span 548 pages, and 13-line prints span 848 pages."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How many Sajdah Tilawat are in the Quran and which is the first Sajdah?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"There are 14 agreed-upon Sajdah Tilawat (prostrations of recitation) in the Holy Quran according to the Hanafi, Shafi’i, and Hanbali schools. The first sajdah in Quran occurs in Surah Al-A’raf (Chapter 7, Verse 206) in Para 9."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What is the shortest surah in the Holy Quran?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"The shortest surah in the Holy Quran is Surah Al-Kawthar (Chapter 108). It consists of only 3 verses (ayat), 10 Arabic words, and 42 letters. It was revealed to comfort the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) with the promise of divine abundance."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What is Dua Khatam Quran and when should it be recited?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Dua Khatam Quran is the traditional supplication recited upon concluding the recitation of the entire Quran (from Surah Al-Fatiha to Surah An-Nas). Scholars note that prayers offered at the completion of a Quran recitation are answered with divine mercy and forgiveness."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What is tagging Al Quran and how does it assist in daily reflection?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Tagging Al Quran is a contemporary study method where readers use color-coded bookmarks and sticky notes to categorize verses by themes such as Dua, Sabr (patience), Tawakkul (trust), Jannah, family ethics, and rulings. It encourages active reflection (Tadabbur) alongside daily recitation."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Where can I read Tafhimul Quran Bangla and access Quran Shikkha or eLearning?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Tafhimul Quran Bangla (Sayyid Abul A’la Maududi’s commentary translated into Bengali) is available across major Islamic learning portals. For beginners and children, Quran Shikkha modules provide phonetics-based Noorani Qaida training, while modern eLearning Quran academies offer one-on-one virtual Tajweed tutoring globally."}}]}7:["$","script",null,{"type":"application/ld+json","dangerouslySetInnerHTML":{"__html":"$c"}}]
