ull,{"className":"p-5 rounded-2xl bg-slate-50 dark:bg-slate-800/60 border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-700/60 space-y-2","children":[["$","h3",null,{"className":"font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-slate-100 text-base","children":"Quran Shikkha Programs"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400 leading-relaxed","children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Quran shikkha"}]," represents systematic foundational learning starting with Noorani Qaida, articulation points (Makharij), short vowels, and essential Tajweed rules tailored for young children and adult beginners."]}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"p-5 rounded-2xl bg-slate-50 dark:bg-slate-800/60 border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-700/60 space-y-2","children":[["$","h3",null,{"className":"font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-slate-100 text-base","children":"eLearning Quran Platforms"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400 leading-relaxed","children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"eLearning quran"}]," connects students globally with certified Al-Azhar and Madinah graduates via video classrooms, enabling flexible Hifz tracking, interactive Tajweed feedback, and accessible Quran education worldwide."]}]]}]]}]]}]
19:["$","$L55",null,{"items":[{"question":"How many total Paras (Juz) and pages are in the Holy Quran?","answer":"The Holy Quran contains 30 Paras (Juz) and 114 Surahs. In the standard King Fahd Complex Madani Mushaf (15-line Uthmani script), there are exactly 604 pages, structured so that each Juz comprises 20 pages (with the 30th Juz covering 23 pages). Indo-Pak 16-line editions generally span 548 pages, and 13-line prints span 848 pages."},{"question":"How many Sajdah Tilawat are in the Quran and which is the first Sajdah?","answer":"There are 14 agreed-upon Sajdah Tilawat (prostrations of recitation) in the Holy Quran according to the Hanafi, Shafi’i, and Hanbali schools. The first sajdah in Quran occurs in Surah Al-A’raf (Chapter 7, Verse 206) in Para 9."},{"question":"What is the shortest surah in the Holy Quran?","answer":"The shortest surah in the Holy Quran is Surah Al-Kawthar (Chapter 108). It consists of only 3 verses (ayat), 10 Arabic words, and 42 letters. It was revealed to comfort the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) with the promise of divine abundance."},{"question":"What is Dua Khatam Quran and when should it be recited?","answer":"Dua Khatam Quran is the traditional supplication recited upon concluding the recitation of the entire Quran (from Surah Al-Fatiha to Surah An-Nas). Scholars note that prayers offered at the completion of a Quran recitation are answered with divine mercy and forgiveness."},{"question":"What is tagging Al Quran and how does it assist in daily reflection?","answer":"Tagging Al Quran is a contemporary study method where readers use color-coded bookmarks and sticky notes to categorize verses by themes such as Dua, Sabr (patience), Tawakkul (trust), Jannah, family ethics, and rulings. It encourages active reflection (Tadabbur) alongside daily recitation."},{"question":"Where can I read Tafhimul Quran Bangla and access Quran Shikkha or eLearning?","answer":"Tafhimul Quran Bangla (Sayyid Abul A’la Maududi’s commentary translated into Bengali) is available across major Islamic learning portals. For beginners and children, Quran Shikkha modules provide phonetics-based Noorani Qaida training, while modern eLearning Quran academies offer one-on-one virtual Tajweed tutoring globally."}],"title":"Frequently Asked Questions on the Holy Quran"}]
